# Prompt
You are the openspec specification agent for EPAM CLI. Phase core, story MOCK3-1.

LOCATED FIX SITE(S) — traced in this repository before you were asked. Anchor every criterion to the behaviour THIS code produces:
- src/fares.ts :: fareFor — This function computes the fare for a rider. The comparison `rider.age > 65` on line 10 excludes age 65 from the concession tier, causing riders aged exactly 65 to fall through to the base fare. Changing `>` to `>=` makes age 65 satisfy the condition, producing the concession fare as the rules require.
- test/fares.test.ts :: fareFor — This test file exercises fareFor but does not cover age 65 (the boundary). Existing tests use ages 8, 30, and 70. After the production fix, all existing tests still pass, but age 65 remains untested. This file needs no edit (test agent owns it), only verification that existing tests continue to pass.


DECLARED FILES — the actual contents of the files this story names or the detective located. Base every observable criterion on what THIS code does, not on what the title suggests:
--- src/fares.ts
/** Fare rules for a transit line. Ages are whole years. */
export type Rider = { age: number; hasPass: boolean };

export const BASE_FARE_CENTS = 350;
export const CONCESSION_FARE_CENTS = 175;

/** Riders aged 65 AND OVER pay the concession fare. */
export function fareFor(rider: Rider): number {
  if (rider.hasPass) return 0;
  if (rider.age > 65) return CONCESSION_FARE_CENTS;
  if (rider.age < 13) return CONCESSION_FARE_CENTS;
  return BASE_FARE_CENTS;
}

export function totalFor(riders: Rider[]): number {
  return riders.reduce((sum, r) => sum + fareFor(r), 0);
}

--- test/fares.test.ts
import { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest';
import { fareFor, BASE_FARE_CENTS, CONCESSION_FARE_CENTS } from '../src/fares';

describe('fareFor', () => {
  it('charges the base fare for an adult', () => {
    expect(fareFor({ age: 30, hasPass: false })).toBe(BASE_FARE_CENTS);
  });
  it('charges nothing when the rider holds a pass', () => {
    expect(fareFor({ age: 30, hasPass: true })).toBe(0);
  });
  it('charges the concession fare for a child', () => {
    expect(fareFor({ age: 8, hasPass: false })).toBe(CONCESSION_FARE_CENTS);
  });
  it('charges the concession fare well past the senior boundary', () => {
    expect(fareFor({ age: 70, hasPass: false })).toBe(CONCESSION_FARE_CENTS);
  });
});



